WHY — the gap distribution in the corpora themselves
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  BTCUSD   open[t] == close[t-1] exactly on 540 of 3,134 bars (17.2%)
           |gap| in ATR: median 0.0031, p99 0.030, max 1.661   (threshold 0.75)
           |gap| as % of price: median 0.0135%
  ETHUSDT  open[t] == close[t-1] exactly on 702 of 1,460 bars (48.1%)
           |gap| in ATR: median 0.0000, p99 0.000, max 0.003   (threshold 0.75)
           |gap| as % of price: median 0.0002%
  SOLUSDT  open[t] == close[t-1] exactly on 740 of 1,460 bars (50.7%)
           |gap| in ATR: median 0.0000, p99 0.010, max 0.012   (threshold 0.75)
           |gap| as % of price: median 0.0000%

These corpora are 24/7 spot markets. There is no overnight session:
the daily open is the first print after 00:00 UTC and the prior
daily close is the last print before it. The 'gap' this thesis is
about is a tick-level move across midnight, not an auction
discontinuity — so a 0.75-ATR gap is a once-in-a-corpus event.

